Explanation:
The tuned model shows improvement in F1-score and recall compared to the base model, indicating better balance between precision and recall. This suggests that hyperparameter tuning helped the model generalize better.

Hyperparameter:
=>hidden_layer_sizes: Controls the complexity of the neural network. Tried different sizes like (50,), (100,), (50,50) to balance underfitting and overfitting.
=>activation: Tested ‘relu’ and ‘tanh’. ReLU is generally faster and works well for deep networks.
=>solver: ‘adam’ is efficient for large datasets, so it was preferred.
=>alpha: Regularization parameter to reduce overfitting. Smaller values allow flexibility; larger values penalize complexity.
=>learning_rate: Controls how fast the model learns. ‘adaptive’ helps adjust learning during training.

Conclusion:
The tuned MLPClassifier model shows improved performance compared to the base model, particularly in terms of F1-score and recall. This indicates better generalization and improved handling of class imbalance.